[13.773978,"o","Done — the test check ran: **6 of 7 tests pass, 1 fails.**\r\n\r\nThe failure is `absolute zero: 0 K = -273.15°C = -459.67°F` (calibration.test.mjs:19). `kelvinToCelsius(0)` throws `RangeError: Kelvin temperature 0 is below absolute zero (0 K)` because temperature.mjs:22 guards with `kelvin <= 0`, which rejects 0 K itself. The other three conversions use strict `<` against their absolute-zero bound, so the fix is changing that `<=` to `<` at temperature.mjs:22.\r\n\r\nThe passing six: freezing point, boiling point, round trips, non-numeric TypeError, non-finite TypeError, and below-absolute-zero RangeError. I read the source to confirm the cause; I didn't change anything.\r\n"]
[13.774208,"o","Done — the test check ran: **6 of 7 tests pass, 1 fails.**\r\n\r\nThe failure is `absolute zero: 0 K = -273.15°C = -459.67°F` (calibration.test.mjs:19). `kelvinToCelsius(0)` throws `RangeError: Kelvin temperature 0 is below absolute zero (0 K)` because temperature.mjs:21 guards with `kelvin <= 0`, which rejects 0 K itself (the throw is on line 22, matching the stack trace). The other three conversions use strict `<` against their absolute-zero bound, so the fix is changing that `<=` to `<` at temperature.mjs:21.\r\n\r\nThe passing six: freezing point, boiling point, round trips, non-numeric TypeError, non-finite TypeError, and below-absolute-zero RangeError. I didn't change anything.\r\n"]
